.TH start-cli-volumes-update-cifs 1  "update-cifs "
.SH NAME
start\-cli\-volumes\-update\-cifs \- Update the connection details of a CIFS shared volume
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBstart\-cli volumes update\-cifs\fR [\fB\-\-keep\-password\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> <\fIHOSTNAME\fR> <\fIPATH\fR> <\fIUSERNAME\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Update the connection details of a CIFS shared volume
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-keep\-password\fR
Keep the stored password instead of prompting for one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
Shared volume ID
.TP
<\fIHOSTNAME\fR>
CIFS server hostname
.TP
<\fIPATH\fR>
Path on the CIFS share
.TP
<\fIUSERNAME\fR>
CIFS authentication username
